The `--lsp` server answers the requests below. Each has its own page, which links to an example tiddler to open in your editor and try.

!! What it answers

|! Capability |! Request |! What it does |
|[[LSP Completion]] |`textDocument/completion` |Tiddler titles inside `[[...]]` and `{{...}}`, triggered by `[` and `{` |
|[[LSP Diagnostics]] |`textDocument/publishDiagnostics` |Warnings on links and transclusions whose target does not exist |
|[[LSP Hover]] |`textDocument/hover` |What the filter, macro call or widget under the cursor amounts to |
|[[LSP Go to Definition]] |`textDocument/definition` |The `.tid` file behind the link under the cursor |
|[[LSP Find References]] |`textDocument/references` |Every call of the macro, procedure, function or widget under the cursor |

Plus the plumbing those need: `initialize`, full document sync (`didOpen`, `didChange`, `didClose`) so answers cover unsaved text, and `shutdown` / `exit`. On a socket, `exit` ends the connection and leaves the process serving.

Not answered yet: rename, document symbols, semantic tokens, and completion inside widget attributes such as `<$link to="...">`.

